<h3 id="what-moves">What is moving</h3>
<p>ArtStation is moving its marketplace to Gumroad. Your listings and your storefront come to Gumroad, and buyers check out here instead of on ArtStation. ArtStation's Marketplace checkout retires at the end of 2026, and the emails ArtStation sends you carry the exact dates for your storefront.</p>
<p>Nothing is duplicated: once a product is selling on Gumroad, the sale is processed and paid out by Gumroad, and the orders that were placed on ArtStation before your products moved stay with ArtStation.</p>

<h3 id="the-link">Opening the link ArtStation sends you</h3>
<p>ArtStation sends you a one-time link when your storefront is ready to move. Open it and confirm:</p>
<ul>
  <li>If you already have a Gumroad account, sign in to it. Using the email address ArtStation has for you keeps the import attached to the right account.</li>
  <li>If you do not have one, the page offers to create it, and emails you a link to set a password and accept the terms.</li>
</ul>
<p>Confirming is what starts the import, so nothing arrives until you open the link and confirm. The link works once: if yours has expired, ask ArtStation for a new one.</p>

<h3 id="drafts">Your products arrive as drafts</h3>
<p>Every product comes in as a draft with its files, cover and price, and any license options come in as variants. Nothing is published for you. For each draft:</p>
<ul>
  <li>Open it and check the file, the price and the cover.</li>
  <li>Fix anything that did not come across the way you want it, such as a file you replaced on ArtStation since the export.</li>
  <li>Publish it. The product then appears on your Gumroad profile with a Gumroad link you can share.</li>
</ul>
<p>Buyers cannot buy a draft, so a product that has not been published is not for sale yet.</p>

<h3 id="getting-paid">Getting paid</h3>
<p>Gumroad pays you, not ArtStation, for sales made here. Payouts go to the payout method saved in <a href="https://gumroad.com/settings/payments">payments settings</a>. The bank account on your ArtStation account is not carried over, so set your payout method before your first sale.</p>
<p>Payouts then follow the usual Gumroad rules: a $100 USD minimum balance, sales held 7 days before they become eligible, a payout each week that includes sales made through the previous Friday (UTC), and PayPal payouts processed in USD with a 2% fee, usually arriving within 1 to 3 business days. <a href="13-getting-paid">Getting paid</a> has the full schedule and the payout day for your country and method.</p>

<h3 id="india">If your payout method was a bank account in India</h3>
<p>If ArtStation paid you directly into an Indian bank account, that arrangement does not carry over. Direct bank payouts to an Indian bank account cannot be set up on an account created now, which comes from our payment partners rather than from us, and we cannot switch it on manually even with the correct IFSC code and account number. For India, the payout method is PayPal.</p>
<p>To set it up, open Settings, then Payments, choose PayPal, enter the email address of your PayPal account, and click Update settings at the top of the page. A free Personal account is fine and it has to be in your own name. Saving a payout method is also what lets you publish products, so do this before you publish your first draft.</p>
<p>If bank payouts to Indian bank accounts become available for your account later, you can switch back on the same page.</p>

<h3 id="stays">What stays with ArtStation</h3>
<p>Orders placed on ArtStation before the move, and everything attached to them, stay with ArtStation: refunds, chargebacks, tax and any buyer support for them. ArtStation supports those buyers for 60 days after its Marketplace checkout retires. Your past buyers and their order details are not copied into your Gumroad account, so a sale you made on ArtStation does not appear here.</p>

<h3 id="help">If something looks wrong</h3>
<p>If a product arrived with a missing file, a wrong price or the wrong variant, fix it on the draft before you publish, or edit the product afterwards. If a product or a creator record is missing entirely, or the link does not work, email <a href="mailto:support@gumroad.com">support@gumroad.com</a> with the email address on your Gumroad account and the product name, and we will look at the import for you.</p>
